The lua row in the engine table: $(lua chunk[,input]) runs the chunk whole with its
input on stdin, and what it prints is the result. Lua has no cli name and no argv
companion, so the row carries only its entry point.

Lua is the one guest with no main to rename. amk wants the library, so the guest build
skips lua.c and luac.c and compiles guest/lua_main.c in their place, which is where
lua_run_main lives. Lua also ships no configure, so its guest rule compiles the sources
directly instead of running one.

--- a/src/amk.h
+++ b/src/amk.h
@@ -19,5 +19,6 @@

 extern int gawk_main (int argc, char **argv);
 extern int jq_main (int argc, char **argv);
+extern int lua_run_main (int argc, char **argv);

 #endif
--- a/src/function.c
+++ b/src/function.c
@@ -2499,6 +2499,9 @@
 #ifdef AMK_ENGINE_JQ
     { "jq", "jq", jq_main, 0, 0, 1 },
 #endif
+#ifdef AMK_ENGINE_LUA
+    { "lua", 0, lua_run_main, 0, 0, 0 },
+#endif
     { 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 }
   };

